Fixed false positive ``too-few-public-methods`` for classes decorated with
``attr.s``, ``attr.dataclass``, ``attr.define``, ``attrs.mutable`` and the other
``attrs`` class decorators when they are used through ``import attr``, through
an alias, or imported by name. The decorator is now matched by the name it was
imported from, so a local function that happens to be called ``s`` or
``mutable`` is still reported.

Closes #3732
